 r←GetNuGetDependencyFolders config;msg;folder;target
⍝ Returns a vector of (folder target) pairs from the project `config` namespace: one pair when
⍝ "dependencies.nuget" is not empty, otherwise none.
⍝ `folder` is relative to the project folder; `target` is relative to the project space, and empty
⍝ when the packages go into the project space itself.
⍝ "nuget" in "dependencies_dev" is permitted but not supported, so it is ignored.
⍝ Returns a vector rather than a single pair in case that changes one day.
⍝ An invalid setting is signalled as an error.
 r←''
 (msg folder target)←'dependencies.nuget'ParseDependencySetting'dependencies'GetNuGetDependencies config
 msg Assert 0=≢msg
 :If 0<≢folder
     r,←⊂folder target
 :EndIf
⍝Done
